Transistor family
All small‑signal NPN: 2N3904 everywhere (Q1–Q12).

If you want a bit more robustness on the dot driver:

QD1/QD2: 2N2222 instead of 2N3904 (optional).

Core timing (oscillator + dividers)
Master oscillator (Q1 + crystal):

Crystal: 3.579545 MHz NTSC.

Bias resistors:

Rbias1: 1 MΩ from base to collector.

Rbias2: 100 kΩ from base to ground.

Load caps:

C1, C2: 22–33 pF to ground.

Divider chain (Q2–Q5):

Each stage:

Collector resistor: 10 kΩ to +5 V.

Base resistor (from previous stage): 47 kΩ.

Simple RC for shaping if needed: 1 nF to ground at each node.

Frame‑rate taps (approximate)
You’ll pick taps from the divider chain to get:

FR_30: ~30 Hz (divide by ~120 k from 3.58 MHz; you’ll do this in multiple stages).

FR_100: ~100 Hz (different tap).

FR_1000: ~1000 Hz (higher‑frequency tap).

For a first build, don’t chase exact NTSC math—aim for:

Stage 1: ÷10 → ~358 kHz

Stage 2: ÷10 → ~35.8 kHz

Stage 3: ÷10 → ~3.58 kHz

Stage 4: ÷10 → ~358 Hz

Then derive:

FR_30: divide 358 Hz by ~12 (extra small divider or RC gating).

FR_100: use ~100 Hz tap (e.g. divide 358 Hz by ~3.6).

FR_1000: use ~1 kHz from earlier stage (e.g. 3.58 kHz / ~3.6).

You can implement the last “divide by ~3–12” with simple transistor multivibrators or CMOS counters if you want cleaner numbers.

Envelope networks (profiles)
Breathing Field:

R_BREATH: 100 kΩ

C_BREATH: 10 µF

Driven by a low‑frequency oscillator (~0.2–0.5 Hz) or gated frame pulses.

Chromatic Drift:

Same RC as breathing, but used to step LED color selection:

R_DRIFT: 100 kΩ

C_DRIFT: 4.7–10 µF

Ghostwave:

Faster, more stepped envelope:

R_GW: 47 kΩ

C_GW: 4.7 µF

Whiteout:

Very fast rise, short decay:

R_WO: 10 kΩ

C_WO: 1 µF

Selector transistor biasing
For all selector transistors (QM1–QM3, QC0–QC6, QP0–QP3):

Base resistors from MCU pins: 4.7–10 kΩ.

Collector resistors (if needed): 10 kΩ to +5 V.

They act as low‑side switches pulling a network node to ground or enabling it.

Dot driver
QD1 (2N2222 or 2N3904):

Base resistor from LUMA_ENV_OUT: 4.7 kΩ.

Collector: to CRT video input (through resistor).

Emitter: to ground.

Output resistor to CRT video input:

R_DOT: 1 kΩ–2.2 kΩ (start at 1 kΩ, adjust brightness).

If using an LED instead of CRT:

LED + series resistor (e.g. 470–1 kΩ) from +5 V to QD1 collector.

Supply and rails
VCC: +5 V for logic and analog.

If CRT video input expects ~1 Vpp, the 2N3904/2N2222 with 1 kΩ series will be in the right ballpark.
